From f98af0202c7ec9b5b12fc9e88c3275757987fc00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nixpkgs contributors <nixpkgs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:45:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] clang: interpret wrapper frames using native argument
 ownership

Keep raw conditional argument groups separate until native response expansion
and option parsing. A provisional caller-only frontend probe may only reject
a request after expansion has established its stable leading frontend token.
Otherwise the combined driver grammar owns response errors.

Observe invocation-wide compatibility guards for opaque wrapper support
files. These are distinct from native per-job implicit header/library use:
only nostdlib suppresses the opaque C++ link group, while native toolchains
retain ownership of nodefaultlibs, nostdlib++ and Xarch resource behavior.

Configured machine/ABI defaults use native Xarch_host translation after
merged target/config selection; preprocessing retains the configured target.
